{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9xNdiEMztvecqfmibis","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery now handles `http.ErrAbortHandler` panics the same way it handles broken connections. They get a one-line log entry with no stack trace, and the request is aborted with the error recorded instead of getting a 500. The change is in `recovery.go:71`.\n\nI added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` in `recovery_test.go`. Gate passed: the new test fails without the fix and passes with it, and the format checks are clean.\n\n**Not checked:** I didn't run the full test suite. This still logs one line per abort rather than staying completely silent, and it doesn't re-panic so that `net/http` can abort the connection itself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":33024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1250,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":210,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3869cacb-a860-4f81-b184-b3740102df4d","uuid":"84da2a88-4fc7-47e1-9518-f4e95efebe22","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:40:49.873Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9xNdV62kxvZ6LoTDZYC"}
